      "file": "t66.py",
      "line": 13,
      "evidence": "note = request.args.get('note', '')",
      "llm_reasoning": "The 'note' parameter is accepted without length constraints, which could lead to memory exhaustion or UI breakage if an attacker sends an extremely large string.",
      "suggested_fix": "Truncate the note input: note = request.args.get('note', '')[:255]"
